  "chief_complaint": "Evaluation and management of end\u2011stage renal disease (CKD stage 4) while awaiting kidney transplantation",
  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 55\u2011year\u2011old man with a long history of type 2 diabetes mellitus complicated by progressive diabetic nephropathy. Over the past several years his chronic kidney disease has advanced from stage 1 to stage 4, and he was placed on the kidney transplant waiting list in January 2018. He suffered an acute ST\u2011segment elevation myocardial infarction in 2012 and has since been on secondary prevention therapy. He has persistent anemia, proteinuria, hypertriglyceridemia, and obesity (BMI >30). Social factors including chronic stress, social isolation, and limited contact have been documented since 2015, potentially affecting adherence. Recent laboratory data are incomplete; the most recent hemoglobin A1c is recorded as 3.1%, which is likely erroneous. Current medication regimen includes insulin, metformin, aspirin, metoprolol, and high\u2011dose atorvastatin.",
